# Keep the SM8550 thermal sensors from waking the system.
#
# tsens arms its threshold interrupts as wake sources whenever its device may
# wake (tsens_suspend_common). On SM8550 the lower-threshold interrupt fires as
# the SoC cools after suspend entry and resumes it at once (ROCKNIX PR 3126,
# `0203`; Kettle Linux ships the same rule as 60-kettle-tsens-nowake.rules).
# Cost: no thermal wake at all while asleep, critical trips included.
#
# "add" as well as "bind": the driver is built in and binds before udevd starts,
# so coldplug only replays "add" for it (seen on the Retroid Pocket Nova,
# 2026-11-11: with "bind" alone the attribute stayed "enabled").
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", DRIVER=="qcom-tsens", ENV{OF_COMPATIBLE_0}=="qcom,sm8550-tsens", ATTR{power/wakeup}="disabled"
